window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-hirata-yousuke"]=[{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke classroom day 1  initiating class introductions class 1 d classroom after chabashira abruptly leaves  students are in stunned disarray celebrating their 100 000 point deposits without knowing what to do next  stands up with calm confidence  smiling warmly to draw the room s attention   everyone  can you please listen to me for a moment   my name s hirata yousuke  back in junior high  lots of people called me yousuke  feel free to use my first name  i guess my hobby is sports in general  but i especially like soccer  i m planning on playing soccer here  too  nice to meet you  effortlessly breaks the ice  commands widespread admiration  girls in class immediately swoon  proposes orderly self introductions starting from the front row so classmates can learn each other s names before ceremony  natural leader  charismatic  genuinely kind  self effacing  proactive  instinctively steps forward to build group cohesion  warm  gentle  inviting  devoid of ego or condescension","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: initiating class introductions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.32–34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after Chabashira abruptly leaves. Students are in stunned disarray celebrating their 100,000-point deposits without knowing what to do next.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, can you please listen to me for a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name’s Hirata Yousuke. Back in junior high, lots of people called me Yousuke. Feel free to use my first name! I guess my hobby is sports in general, but I especially like soccer. I’m planning on playing soccer here, too. Nice…”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up with calm confidence, smiling warmly to draw the room&#x27;s attention.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My name’s Hirata Yousuke. Back in junior high, lots of people called me Yousuke. Feel free to use my first name! I guess my hobby is sports in general, but I especially like soccer. I’m planning on playing soccer here, too. Nice to meet you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Effortlessly breaks the ice; commands widespread admiration; girls in class immediately swoon. Proposes orderly self-introductions starting from the front row so classmates can learn each other&#x27;s names before ceremony.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Natural leader, charismatic, genuinely kind, self-effacing, proactive; instinctively steps forward to build group cohesion.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Warm, gentle, inviting, devoid of ego or condescension.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\">→ After: Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke mediating sudo s rebellion   koenji s narcissism class 1 d classroom during self introductions  encourages sudo to speak  met with intense delinquent hostility  leave me out of it   i can t force you to introduce yourself  of course  however  i don t think that getting along with your classmates is a bad thing  if i ve made you uncomfortable  i apologize  bows deeply to sudo  when class girls snap at sudo to defend hirata  hirata immediately takes the blame onto himself to protect class unity   they re not a bad bunch  it s my fault  i was being selfish and made people do this  looks visibly saddened and lonely as horikita  sudo  and others walk out of the room  politely asks koenji to introduce himself  bewildered when koenji puts his feet on his desk and threatens to punish  ugly things   excuse me  can you introduce yourself   um  kouenji kun  what exactly do you mean when you say   anyone who makes me uncomfortable   ah  thank you  i will be careful then   handles koenji s bizarre threat with polite  defusing compliance  gently supports ayanokoji after he stumbles and freezes during his own botched introduction  peacemaker to a fault  absorbs blame to de escalate tension  refuses to cast out delinquents or oddballs  desperate to keep everyone together  patient and forgiving despite sudo s hostility  courteous handling of an uncontrollable eccentric  encouraging classmate  attempts to welcome him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.37–40<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom during self-introductions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t force you to introduce yourself, of course. However, I don’t think that getting along with your classmates is a bad thing. If I’ve made you uncomfortable, I apologize.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“They’re not a bad bunch. It’s my fault. I was being selfish and made people do this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Excuse me, can you introduce yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Encourages Sudō to speak; met with intense delinquent hostility (&quot;Leave me out of it&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bows deeply to Sudō. When class girls snap at Sudō to defend Hirata, Hirata immediately takes the blame onto himself to protect class unity.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Looks visibly saddened and lonely as Horikita, Sudō, and others walk out of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Politely asks Kōenji to introduce himself; bewildered when Kōenji puts his feet on his desk and threatens to punish &quot;ugly things&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, Kouenji-kun. What exactly do you mean when you say, ‘anyone who makes me uncomfortable’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, thank you. I will be careful then.” (handles Kōenji&#x27;s bizarre threat with polite, defusing compliance).<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gently supports Ayanokōji after he stumbles and freezes during his own botched introduction.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Peacemaker to a fault; absorbs blame to de-escalate tension; refuses to cast out delinquents or oddballs; desperate to keep everyone together.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Patient and forgiving despite Sudō&#x27;s hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Courteous handling of an uncontrollable eccentric.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Encouraging classmate, attempts to welcome him.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: initiating class introductions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\">→ After: The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the cafeteria invitation   female popularity class 1 d classroom at lunch bell  day 2  stands up to invite any lonely or unacquainted classmates to head to the cafeteria together   well  i was thinking of heading to the cafeteria  anyone want to come with me   does anyone else want to come  swarmed immediately by eager female classmates who prevent other quiet boys from speaking up  hirata spots ayanokoji lingering alone with his hand partially raised and begins to call out his name  but a fashionista girl  karuizawa kei  latches onto his arm and whisks him away to lunch  leaving ayanokoji behind  actively looks out for isolated students  but his immense popularity with the girls accidentally hinders him from rescuing quiet male classmates  early dynamic  she latches onto his arm as the class s top status boy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.55–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom at lunch bell, Day 2.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I was thinking of heading to the cafeteria. Anyone want to come with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Does anyone else want to come?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up to invite any lonely or unacquainted classmates to head to the cafeteria together.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Swarmed immediately by eager female classmates who prevent other quiet boys from speaking up. Hirata spots Ayanokōji lingering alone with his hand partially raised and begins to call out his name, but a fashionista girl (Karuizawa Kei) latches onto his arm and whisks him away to lunch, leaving Ayanokōji behind.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Actively looks out for isolated students, but his immense popularity with the girls accidentally hinders him from rescuing quiet male classmates.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Early dynamic: she latches onto his arm as the class&#x27;s top status boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\">← Before: Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\">→ After: Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke athletic swimming demonstration   universal kindness indoor swimming pool  swims against sudo in the second boys  heat  displays clean  graceful athletic technique  finishing just behind sudo s raw power in approximately 26 seconds  swarmed with compliments by class girls  you re not just good at soccer  you re really good at swimming   you think so  thank you  stares in amazement when koenji records a blazing 23 22 seconds in the subsequent heat  well rounded athletic ability beyond his primary sport  soccer  humble and courteous recipient of female praise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.85–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Indoor swimming pool.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You think so? Thank you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Swims against Sudō in the second boys&#x27; heat; displays clean, graceful athletic technique, finishing just behind Sudō&#x27;s raw power in approximately 26 seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Swarmed with compliments by class girls (*&quot;You&#x27;re not just good at soccer, you&#x27;re really good at swimming!&quot;*).<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stares in amazement when Kōenji records a blazing 23.22 seconds in the subsequent heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Well-rounded athletic ability beyond his primary sport (soccer); humble and courteous recipient of female praise.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\">← Before: The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\">→ After: Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke anti bullying vigil   horikita s isolation classroom 1 d after class  intercepts ayanokoji in the classroom with pure  earnest concern   it s about horikita san  actually  i was wondering if something was wrong  some of the girls were talking about it earlier  horikita always seems to be alone   could you possibly tell her to try to get along with people a little   you re right  of course  however  many people have voiced their concerns about it  i absolutely do not want any bullying in our class  extreme sensitivity to social friction  hyper vigilant against potential ostracization or bullying before it even begins  concerned for her safety and integration despite her prickly demeanor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.90<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D after class.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s about Horikita-san, actually. I was wondering if something was wrong. Some of the girls were talking about it earlier. Horikita always seems to be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could you possibly tell her to try to get along with people a little?”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right, of course. However, many people have voiced their concerns about it. I absolutely do not want any bullying in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Intercepts Ayanokōji in the classroom with pure, earnest concern.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Extreme sensitivity to social friction; hyper-vigilant against potential ostracization or bullying before it even begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Concerned for her safety and integration despite her prickly demeanor.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\">← Before: Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\">→ After: Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke dating karuizawa   moral unease over point lavishness classroom 1 d  then boutique and cafe in keyaki mall  revealed to be dating class 1 d s fashionista girl  karuizawa kei  cementing their standing as the premier couple of the class  accompanies karuizawa on a shopping spree in keyaki mall  patiently carrying her shopping bags filled with  30 000 points of designer clothes   don t you think it s abnormal for a high school student to get 300 000 points as a monthly allowance  expresses genuine moral and practical concern over the school s financial indulgence  worries that receiving  100 000 monthly will ruin the students  sense of financial discipline and cripple their ability to survive in normal society after graduation  grounded  socially conscientious  deeply resistant to superficial materialism  looks ahead to real world consequences after high school  gentle  accommodating boyfriend  caters to her luxury shopping while maintaining his own level headed values","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.103, 117–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; then boutique and café in Keyaki Mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you think it’s abnormal for a high school student to get 300,000 points as a monthly allowance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Revealed to be dating Class 1-D&#x27;s fashionista girl, Karuizawa Kei, cementing their standing as the premier couple of the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accompanies Karuizawa on a shopping spree in Keyaki Mall, patiently carrying her shopping bags filled with ~30,000 points of designer clothes.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Expresses genuine moral and practical concern over the school&#x27;s financial indulgence; worries that receiving ¥100,000 monthly will ruin the students&#x27; sense of financial discipline and cripple their ability to survive in normal society after graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grounded, socially conscientious; deeply resistant to superficial materialism; looks ahead to real-world consequences after high school.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Gentle, accommodating boyfriend; caters to her luxury shopping while maintaining his own level-headed values.<span class=\"pg\">p.103, 117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\">← Before: Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\">→ After: Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke standing up for the class   the podium appeal classroom 1 d  may 1st morning homeroom and subsequent class chaos  takes the initiative on behalf of the bewildered class to question chabashira regarding the missing points   sensei  may i please ask you a question  i m afraid i still don t understand  can you please tell us why we didn t receive any points  we won t completely understand otherwise  politely challenges chabashira s omission of point deduction rules   chiyabashira sensei  i do not recall hearing you explain that to us before  of course  there was never any talk about reducing our points  had that been explained beforehand  i m sure we would have avoided being late or talking during class   well then  could you at least explain in detail how points are added or deducted  we can keep that in mind for future reference  expression darkens as chabashira reveals that merely eliminating infractions will still leave them at zero points next month  when the classroom descends into panic during the break  hirata steps in to soothe tempers  yukimura grabs his collar in a rage  hirata remains completely non violent   i understand that you re all confused right now  but everyone needs to calm down  even if i was  isn t it better for us to band together so we can turn things around  i understand  however  sitting here whining won t help us right now  after kushida defuses yukimura  hirata takes accountability gracefully   it s all right  i should have chosen my words a little more carefully  takes the teacher s podium before next period to deliver an impassioned call for class unity   attention  everyone  before class begins  i want you to listen seriously for a moment  especially you  sudou kun  we didn t get any points this month  this is a serious problem  and one that will have an enormous impact on our daily lives moving forward  it s impossible for us to make it to graduation with zero points  right   of course  therefore  we must earn points next month  to do that  we all need to cooperate with each other  so  please  take care not to be late to class or to talk during the lecture  also  the use of cell phones during class is prohibited  of course   as long as we continue talking during class and being late  our points won t increase for sure  although we can t go below zero points  disruption will  without a doubt  count as strikes against us  when sudo aggressively rejects his appeal  hirata bows his head with courteous humility rather than getting angry   i don t think that there s anything particularly wrong with what you said  sudou kun  i apologize if i made you feel uncomfortable   bows his head politely toward the disgruntled sudou   however  sudou kun  it s a fact that unless we all cooperate  we won t get any more points  steps down from the podium and stops directly in front of horikita and ayanokoji s desks to personally recruit them into a collective study and improvement effort   horikita san  ayanokouji kun  do you have a moment  i want to speak with you about how we can increase our points  i d like you to join me   this is the first trial we re facing together as a united class d  so then  when horikita rejects him outright  i refuse  i won t participate  hirata accepts her rebuff with a self deprecating wry smile rather than anger   i i see  i m sorry  if you change your mind  i d love for you to join us   what about you  ayanokouji kun   no  i m sorry for bothering you  if you change your mind  please let me know  quintessential servant leader  absorbs class hostility without retaliation  persistent dedication to total class unity even when facing toxic rebuffs  patiently mediates sudo s outbursts without malice  tries earnestly to draw her into the fold  bears her scorn with diplomatic grace  values his quiet presence  extends an open door invitation without coercion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.121–125, 131–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st morning homeroom and subsequent class chaos.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sensei, may I please ask you a question? I’m afraid I still don’t understand… Can you please tell us why we didn’t receive any points? We won’t completely understand otherwise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chiyabashira-sensei. I do not recall hearing you explain that to us before… Of course. There was never any talk about reducing our points. Had that been explained beforehand, I’m sure we would have avoided being late or talking…”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well then, could you at least explain in detail how points are added or deducted? We can keep that in mind for future reference.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the initiative on behalf of the bewildered class to question Chabashira regarding the missing points.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Politely challenges Chabashira’s omission of point deduction rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Chiyabashira-sensei. I do not recall hearing you explain that to us before… Of course. There was never any talk about reducing our points. Had that been explained beforehand, I’m sure we would have avoided being late or talking during class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Expression darkens as Chabashira reveals that merely eliminating infractions will still leave them at zero points next month.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the classroom descends into panic during the break, Hirata steps in to soothe tempers. Yukimura grabs his collar in a rage; Hirata remains completely non-violent.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that you’re all confused right now, but everyone needs to calm down… Even if I was, isn’t it better for us to band together so we can turn things around?… I understand. However, sitting here whining won’t help us right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Kushida defuses Yukimura, Hirata takes accountability gracefully.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s all right. I should have chosen my words a little more carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the teacher’s podium before next period to deliver an impassioned call for class unity.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Attention, everyone. Before class begins, I want you to listen seriously for a moment. Especially you, Sudou-kun… We didn’t get any points this month. This is a serious problem, and one that will have an enormous impact on our daily lives moving forward. It’s impossible for us to make it to graduation with zero points, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Therefore, we must earn points next month. To do that, we all need to cooperate with each other. So, please, take care not to be late to class or to talk during the lecture. Also, the use of cell phones during class is prohibited, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As long as we continue talking during class and being late, our points won’t increase for sure. Although we can’t go below zero points, disruption will, without a doubt, count as strikes against us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō aggressively rejects his appeal, Hirata bows his head with courteous humility rather than getting angry.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think that there’s anything particularly wrong with what you said, Sudou-kun. I apologize if I made you feel uncomfortable.” (bows his head politely toward the disgruntled Sudou)<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, Sudou-kun, it’s a fact that unless we all cooperate, we won’t get any more points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps down from the podium and stops directly in front of Horikita and Ayanokōji’s desks to personally recruit them into a collective study and improvement effort.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun, do you have a moment? I want to speak with you about how we can increase our points. I’d like you to join me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the first trial we’re facing together as a united Class D. So then—”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Horikita rejects him outright (“I refuse. I won’t participate.”), Hirata accepts her rebuff with a self-deprecating wry smile rather than anger.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…I see. I’m sorry. If you change your mind, I’d love for you to join us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about you, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m sorry for bothering you. If you change your mind, please let me know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quintessential servant-leader; absorbs class hostility without retaliation; persistent dedication to total class unity even when facing toxic rebuffs.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Patiently mediates Sudō&#x27;s outbursts without malice.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Tries earnestly to draw her into the fold; bears her scorn with diplomatic grace.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Values his quiet presence; extends an open-door invitation without coercion.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, 137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\">← Before: Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: The midterm study group announcement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the midterm study group announcement classroom 1 d  lunchtime  takes the floor when everyone rises for lunch and announces his own study group project  staring directly at sudou during his grand speech   chiyabashira sensei mentioned that the midterm is coming up soon  remember that if you fail  you ll be expelled  therefore  i think it would be a good idea to form a study group   if you neglect your studies  you ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot  i want to avoid that  however  studying won t just prevent expulsion  it may also help earn points  if we receive high marks  our class s assessment should improve as a result  i asked some of the students who scored high on the test to help prepare a study plan  so  i would like people who are anxious to come join our group  everyone is welcome  of course   starting today at five o clock  we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test  if you d like to join us  please come whenever you like  of course  i don t mind if you need to leave partway  that s all i have to say  several failing students immediately get up and join  sudou  ike  and yamauchi notably stay seated   the three he most wanted  especially sudou  proactive crisis leadership paired with personal charisma  his group becomes the default destination for the class s struggling students  relationship rocky since sudou stomped all over his introduction game  targets sudou with a direct stare during the speech  but sudou averts his gaze in a tch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The midterm study group announcement<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152–156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, lunchtime.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chiyabashira-sensei mentioned that the midterm is coming up soon. Remember that if you fail, you’ll be expelled. Therefore, I think it would be a good idea to form a study group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you neglect your studies, you’ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot. I want to avoid that. However, studying won’t just prevent expulsion; it may also help earn points. If we receive high marks, our class’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Starting today at five o’clock, we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test. If you’d like to join us, please come whenever you like. Of course, I don’t mind if you need to leave partway. That’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the floor when everyone rises for lunch and announces his own study group project, staring directly at Sudou during his grand speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you neglect your studies, you’ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot. I want to avoid that. However, studying won’t just prevent expulsion; it may also help earn points. If we receive high marks, our class’s assessment should improve as a result. I asked some of the students who scored high on the test to help prepare a study plan. So, I would like people who are anxious to come join our group. Everyone is welcome, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Starting today at five o’clock, we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test. If you’d like to join us, please come whenever you like. Of course, I don’t mind if you need to leave partway. That’s all I have to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Several failing students immediately get up and join; Sudou, Ike, and Yamauchi notably stay seated — the three he most wanted (especially Sudou).<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proactive crisis leadership paired with personal charisma; his group becomes the default destination for the class&#x27;s struggling students.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Relationship rocky since Sudou stomped all over his introduction game; targets Sudou with a direct stare during the speech, but Sudou averts his gaze in a Tch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\">← Before: Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\">→ After: The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the avoided rival   the beneficiary of the test change notice unseen presence shaping logistics  his own study group meets during lunch  which is the main reason horikita s group relocates to the library   she absolutely does not want contact with his group  designated by ayanokoji  via kushida  as a recipient of chabashira s revised test material list  ensuring his larger group also studies the right topics","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.213, 226<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Unseen presence shaping logistics: his own study group meets during lunch, which is the main reason Horikita&#x27;s group relocates to the library — she absolutely does not want contact with his group.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Designated by Ayanokōji (via Kushida) as a recipient of Chabashira&#x27;s revised test-material list, ensuring his larger group also studies the right topics.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: The midterm study group announcement<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\">→ After: Exam-morning confidence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke exam morning confidence answers chabashira s exam day roll call with public confidence in the class   we ve studied diligently these past few weeks  i don t think that anyone will fail  drawn out by her   oh my  you sound quite confident  hirata","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exam-morning confidence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’ve studied diligently these past few weeks. I don’t think that anyone will fail.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Answers Chabashira&#x27;s exam-day roll call with public confidence in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Drawn out by her: “Oh my. You sound quite confident, Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\">← Before: The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: The first to protest the red line<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the first to protest the red line presses chabashira for the results announcement and is calmly brushed off  you should have passed quite easily  first to challenge sudou s expulsion   even though sudou hates him   demanding the answer sheet be audited  verifies every problem himself   s sensei  is sudou kun really being expelled  is there no way to save him   could we possibly see sudou kun s answer sheet   there are no mistakes   his darkening expression after the full audit  moral consistency under hostility  fights for the classmate who insulted him while others silently feel relieved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The first to protest the red line<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246–248<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“S-sensei. Is Sudou-kun really being expelled? Is there no way to save him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could we possibly see Sudou-kun’s answer sheet?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There…are no mistakes.” (his darkening expression after the full audit)<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Presses Chabashira for the results announcement and is calmly brushed off (&quot;You should have passed quite easily&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> First to challenge Sudou&#x27;s expulsion — even though Sudou hates him — demanding the answer sheet be audited; verifies every problem himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Moral consistency under hostility: fights for the classmate who insulted him while others silently feel relieved.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\">← Before: Exam-morning confidence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 1  decoding horikita in public  the class leader  hirata yousuke  answered for her    after horikita bait and silences the class on  get something   i believe that horikita san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout april and may  in other words  we didn t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late  reads peers  half thoughts accurately and translates them for the room without seeking credit  ak   the sharp witted hirata hadn t missed a beat  splendid  named by ak as an expert advice pillar  if it were horikita or hirata here  they d probably be able to give expert advice    but unusable on sudou s case because  sudou hates hirata  still the object of sudou s hatred from the fake expulsion episode  hirata is not in the crisis s inner circle at all  ak holds him up as the standard he himself declines to be","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;The class leader, Hirata Yousuke, answered for her.&quot; — after Horikita bait-and-silences the class on &quot;get something.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I believe that Horikita-san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout April and May. In other words, we didn’t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads peers&#x27; half-thoughts accurately and translates them for the room without seeking credit; AK: &quot;The sharp-witted Hirata hadn’t missed a beat. Splendid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Named by AK as an expert-advice pillar (&quot;If it were Horikita or Hirata here, they’d probably be able to give expert advice.&quot;) — but unusable on Sudou&#x27;s case because &quot;Sudou hates Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Still the object of Sudou&#x27;s hatred from the fake-expulsion episode; Hirata is not in the crisis&#x27;s inner circle at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK holds him up as the standard he himself declines to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  the one standing voice for sudou  umm  so why hasn t this issue been resolved already    ak calls it  a rather reasonable question  the first thing anyone asks chabashira after the announcement   i want to believe him   if a student in another class were casting doubt on him  i could understand it   but i think it s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away  shouldn t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need  stands in support of kushida s appeal for sudou   hirata  the class hero  uttered those words as he stood in support of kushida  his appearance was dashing  and he clearly wasn t drunk on the same anti sudou kool aid as everyone else  his stance converts the room by example  not argument   ak   starting with those three  we launched our investigation to prove sudou s innocence  and  hirata  kushida  and karuizawa had attracted the rest of our class s admiration  the conversion is fragile and ak says so plainly   though they probably mocked him in their hearts  they would help sudou a little bit    the class follows the lead  it does not change its opinion  after school he organizes the canvassing as a team  ak names  the hero   gal team  that he leads with karuizawa  searching campus themselves  publicly defends the classmate who refuses him privately  the year 1  vol  2 ch2 note stands   sudou will not ask him  so the defence costs hirata nothing with sudou and gains sudou nothing with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands in support of Kushida&#x27;s appeal for Sudou: &quot;Hirata, the class hero, uttered those words as he stood in support of Kushida. His appearance was dashing, and he clearly wasn’t drunk on the same anti-Sudou Kool-Aid as everyone else.&quot; After school he organizes the canvassing as a team: AK names &quot;the Hero &amp; Gal Team&quot; that he leads with Karuizawa, searching campus themselves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Umm. So why hasn’t this issue been resolved already?” — AK calls it &quot;a rather reasonable question&quot;, the first thing anyone asks Chabashira after the announcement.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to believe him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If a student in another class were casting doubt on him, I could understand it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I think it’s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away. Shouldn’t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His stance converts the room by example, not argument — AK: &quot;Starting with those three, we launched our investigation to prove Sudou’s innocence&quot;, and &quot;Hirata, Kushida, and Karuizawa had attracted the rest of our class’s admiration.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The conversion is fragile and AK says so plainly: &quot;Though they probably mocked him in their hearts, they would help Sudou a little bit&quot; — the class follows the lead, it does not change its opinion.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Publicly defends the classmate who refuses him privately; the Year 1, Vol. 2 ch2 note stands — Sudou will not ask him, so the defence costs Hirata nothing with Sudou and gains Sudou nothing with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 0  the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has his team s canvass produced records  not results   i heard that hirata and his group hadn t obtained any valuable information  they d recorded the names of the people to whom they d spoken  and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones   then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again    and the reason he gives   it s only been three months since we started here    ak   our classroom hero didn t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech  the girls immediately blushed in response   i understand how you feel  however  it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality  the most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible  the cost of that line on himself  watched by the class s worst judge   ike  who considered hirata a goody two shoes  eyed him suspiciously   even if sudou was at fault    however  hirata nodded without a moment s hesitation  it was as though he believed self sacrifice was unimportant  ike immediately looked downward  as if pressed under the weight of hirata s noble intentions   you know  if you think back on it now  it was obvious from the start    the one student who had already connected the school s signals   remember what our p e  instructor higashiyama sensei said when we went to the pool  he said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points  that was a stepping stone to prepare us for other opportunities  it seems plausible  right  his memory of a teacher s throwaway promise is the evidence that the club points track exists  and ike cannot supply any of it   ike scratched his head and slumped   i don t remember  he said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–72<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His team&#x27;s canvass produced records, not results: &quot;I heard that Hirata and his group hadn’t obtained any valuable information. They’d recorded the names of the people to whom they’d spoken, and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones.&quot; The cost of that line on himself, watched by the class&#x27;s worst judge: &quot;Ike, who considered Hirata a goody two shoes, eyed him suspiciously. &#x27;Even if Sudou was at fault?&#x27; ... However, Hirata nodded without a moment’s hesitation. It was as though he believed self-sacrifice was unimportant. Ike immediately looked downward, as if pressed under the weight of Hirata’s noble intentions.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech.…<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand how you feel. However, it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality. The most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He…<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech. The girls immediately blushed in response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points. That was a stepping stone to prepare us for other opportunities. It seems plausible, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His memory of a teacher&#x27;s throwaway promise is the evidence that the club-points track exists, and Ike cannot supply any of it: &quot;Ike scratched his head and slumped. &#x27;I don’t remember,&#x27; he said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 2 4 3  he will greet sakura but not ask her  and he physically stops sudou  good morning  ayanokouji kun     hirata called to me  his expression as fresh and friendly as usual  the sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him  why he does not go to the witness himself   me  no  i m going to greet her  that s all  i ve wanted to talk to her since she s always by herself  but as a guy i don t want to come off as forceful or anything  also  if i asked karuizawa san to talk with her  that might cause a few problems   i think that for the time being  we ll just wait for more information from kushida san    the hero s plan is to let someone else do the asking  his reason for briefing ak at all   not for any particular reason  i guess it s because you have a connection to horikita san  she doesn t talk to anyone except for you  so i thought you d pass it along    ak   there was no real reason for him to tell me any of this  i wasn t really part of the team  he invites ak into his own social life  girlfriend included   oh  that reminds me  if you re up for it  we should hang out sometime soon  what do you think  and  are you fine with my girlfriend coming  too    and reads ak s refusal when ak himself cannot   i m sorry  do you not really want to  when sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on koenji  he is the only one who moves   he was the only boy able to move in this awful situation  my heart pounded in my chest   all right  that s enough  calm down  you two    and he puts the blame on both sides in front of the class   sudou kun  you certainly are part of the problem here  but kouenji kun  you re in the wrong  too   stop it already  i don t want to see my friends fight  is kushida s  his is the follow up that picks a side for the record   it s just like kushida says  i don t know about kouenji kun  but i m your ally  sudou kun    ak   hirata was way too cool  it would ve been fitting if he changed his name to  hero  his last line to sudou is the school s argument  not his own feeling   i m going to stop this  sudou kun  you should act more mature  if you cause another huge disturbance  the school s evaluation of you will only worsen  right  then  alone with koenji after sudou slams out   kouenji kun  i don t intend to compel you to help  but you were wrong to blame him    and ak s conclusion from watching the pair   watching their bizarre interaction unfold  i realized that our class lacked unity  he never asks the witness anything  never challenges horikita s write off of sudou  and stops a fight by citing the school s evaluation   leadership that avoids being the one who pressures anyone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.83–84, p.92–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He invites AK into his own social life, girlfriend included: &quot;Oh, that reminds me. If you’re up for it, we should hang out sometime soon. What do you think?&quot; and &quot;Are you fine with my girlfriend coming, too?&quot; — and reads AK&#x27;s refusal when AK himself cannot: &quot;I’m sorry. Do you not really want to?&quot; When Sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on Kōenji, he is the only one who moves: &quot;He was the only boy able to move in this awful situation. My heart pounded in my chest.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — &quot;Hirata called to me, his expression as fresh and friendly as usual. The sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked…<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think that for the time being, we’ll just wait for more information from Kushida-san.&quot; — the hero&#x27;s plan is to let someone else do the asking.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked Karuizawa-san to talk with her, that might cause a few problems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His reason for briefing AK at all: &quot;Not for any particular reason. I guess it’s because you have a connection to Horikita-san. She doesn’t talk to anyone except for you, so I thought you’d pass it along.&quot; — AK: &quot;There was no real reason for him to tell me any of this. I wasn’t really part of the team.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;All right, that’s enough. Calm down, you two,&quot; — and he puts the blame on both sides in front of the class: &quot;Sudou-kun. You certainly are part of the problem here. But Kouenji-kun, you’re in the wrong, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stop it already. I don’t want to see my friends fight…&quot; is Kushida&#x27;s; his is the follow-up that picks a side for the record: &quot;It’s just like Kushida says. I don’t know about Kouenji-kun, but I’m your ally, Sudou-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Hirata was way too cool. It would’ve been fitting if he changed his name to &#x27;Hero.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His last line to Sudou is the school&#x27;s argument, not his own feeling: &quot;I’m going to stop this. Sudou-kun, you should act more mature. If you cause another huge disturbance, the school’s evaluation of you will only worsen. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then, alone with Kōenji after Sudou slams out: &quot;Kouenji-kun. I don’t intend to compel you to help. But you were wrong to blame him.&quot; — and AK&#x27;s conclusion from watching the pair: &quot;Watching their bizarre interaction unfold, I realized that our class lacked unity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He never asks the witness anything, never challenges Horikita&#x27;s write-off of Sudou, and stops a fight by citing the school&#x27;s evaluation — leadership that avoids being the one who pressures anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 7   4 11  he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly kushida  on the phone about the corridor fight   i couldn t even move  hirata kun was so amazing  though    ayanokoji s jealous gloss on the praise   hearing her praise hirata like that made me a little jealous  the couple the class copies   it seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like hirata and karuizawa  he is invoked as a teacher of social technique by the one person who watches him most closely   what should i do  please  hirata  teach me  she credits him and herself  in the same breath  for class d s cohesion   class d was able to come together  thanks to you and hirata  in the second half of chapter 4 he appears only as other students  measure of themselves  his own scenes ended at p 93","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.120, p.149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Kushida, on the phone about the corridor fight: &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot; — Ayanokōji&#x27;s jealous gloss on the praise: &quot;Hearing her praise Hirata like that made me a little jealous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The couple the class copies: &quot;It seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like Hirata and Karuizawa.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is invoked as a teacher of social technique by the one person who watches him most closely: &quot;What should I do? Please, Hirata. Teach me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She credits him and herself, in the same breath, for Class D&#x27;s cohesion: &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> In the second half of Chapter 4 he appears only as other students&#x27; measure of themselves; his own scenes ended at p.93.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 7  a passing mention in the verdict he is named once  in horikita s summary of pending rewards for the hearing   kushida s and his actions  would be rewarded as well    and appears nowhere else in the chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is named once, in Horikita’s summary of pending rewards for the hearing — Kushida’s and his actions &quot;would be rewarded as well&quot; — and appears nowhere else in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 0 2 2  the leader tries to hold a class that won t hold still deck of the liner  he pulls ayanokoji into the group the moment he appears  called over as rescue  hirata himself is too busy    miyake kun looks like he s having trouble    and leaves for the cabins  asked why he isn t with her   we just kind of take things at our own pace  reads the watch rule as safety kit  not control   the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe  opened the rules huddle that ike s complaints fracture into factions  breaks his own neutrality on the toilet   i ve thought it over  and i believe we should install one toilet first    then beats yukimura s objection with the arithmetic of thirty plus students sharing one box  the chapter s verdict on the method   it wasn t just to provoke arguments  he was convinced that he d get their approval eventually","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.16, p.30–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he pulls Ayanokōji into the group the moment he appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Called over as rescue; Hirata himself is too busy — &quot;Miyake-kun looks like he&#x27;s having trouble&quot; — and leaves for the cabins.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Asked why he isn&#x27;t with her: “We just kind of take things at our own pace.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads the watch rule as safety kit, not control: &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Opened the rules huddle that Ike&#x27;s complaints fracture into factions.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Breaks his own neutrality on the toilet: &quot;I&#x27;ve thought it over, and I believe we should install one toilet first&quot; — then beats Yukimura&#x27;s objection with the arithmetic of thirty-plus students sharing one box.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s verdict on the method: &quot;It wasn’t just to provoke arguments; he was convinced that he’d get their approval eventually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river  the 120 point speech  and taking ibuki in receives ike s river report and moves the class toward a base camp  praised the find    amazing  ike kun    then takes his name to chabashira as leader candidate filing errand boy  files horikita s name and hands her the card  orchestrates the fake collective touch to hide the leader  breaks up the ike shinohara round two and buys time   let s try breaking apart for a bit  we still have some time  asks ayanokoji for branches  apologetically    i can t force you to agree    because light is necessary whether or not points get spent  the chapter s centrepiece speech  sets the realistic floor at 120 points left  walks the class through the meal maths  10 point sets  12 meals  120 points  then reframes endurance as upside    if we can find drinking water for the week  we ll save fifty points or more  ayanokoji s read   anyone else could have come up with this  but hirata s tone and presentation sold it  he d performed flawlessly  takes the injured class c girl in   we can t just leave someone in trouble  we all think so    and turns the spy question on its head   if you really were a spy  you wouldn t want to be chased out  would you  leaves sakura out of the ibuki escort   ayanokoji reads it as pretty boy thoughtfulness  distributes the evening meal while kushida feeds ibuki from her own group s portion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Receives Ike&#x27;s river report and moves the class toward a base camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Praised the find — &quot;Amazing, Ike-kun!&quot; — then takes his name to Chabashira as leader-candidate filing errand-boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Files Horikita&#x27;s name and hands her the card; orchestrates the fake collective touch to hide the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Breaks up the Ike–Shinohara round two and buys time: &quot;Let’s try breaking apart for a bit. We still have some time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Asks Ayanokōji for branches, apologetically — &quot;I can’t force you to agree&quot; — because light is necessary whether or not points get spent.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s centrepiece speech: sets the realistic floor at 120 points left, walks the class through the meal maths (10-point sets, 12 meals, 120 points), then reframes endurance as upside — &quot;If we can find drinking water for the week, we’ll save fifty points or more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s read: &quot;Anyone else could have come up with this, but Hirata’s tone and presentation sold it. He’d performed flawlessly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Takes the injured Class C girl in: &quot;We can’t just leave someone in trouble. We all think so.&quot; — and turns the spy question on its head: &quot;If you really were a spy, you wouldn’t want to be chased out, would you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves Sakura out of the Ibuki escort — Ayanokōji reads it as pretty-boy thoughtfulness.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Distributes the evening meal while Kushida feeds Ibuki from her own group&#x27;s portion.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  the morning watch and the point arithmetic awake before the class in the crowded tent  greets ayanokoji slipping out  his back aching without a mattress   if you include kouenji kun s penalty  we spent almost 100 points yesterday  i told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we d be left with 120 points  but now i m not even sure about that  i guess the anxiety woke me   i m only doing this because i like it  if my hard work makes everyone in class happy  then i m satisfied  but it s surprisingly difficult  cannot answer the class a question    that s hard to answer  aiming for the upper classes means forcing everyone  i m sorry  i need to think on it  adjusts his position so ayanokoji can read the manual comfortably    small acts of consideration  noted from the other side  carries her heart bedazzled gifts in his pack and confirms it    spot on  how d you guess  greets kanzaki by name and accepts the apology for the early visit   i wonder if our strategy s wrong  even if we can t beat the other classes  i thought it d be good for us to unify on this test  that s the real reason i don t want them to discover our leader   thank you  coming from you  that honestly makes me really happy  plans the sleeping arrangement poll at the river  then after roll call assigns roles to the reliable students   class d s point saving start","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Awake before the class in the crowded tent; greets Ayanokōji slipping out, his back aching without a mattress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you include Kouenji-kun&#x27;s penalty, we spent almost 100 points yesterday. I told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we&#x27;d be left with 120 points, but now I&#x27;m not even sure about that. I guess the anxiety woke me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m only doing this because I like it. If my hard work makes everyone in class happy, then I&#x27;m satisfied. But it&#x27;s surprisingly difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder if our strategy&#x27;s wrong. Even if we can&#x27;t beat the other classes, I thought it&#x27;d be good for us to unify on this test. That&#x27;s the real reason I don&#x27;t want them to discover our leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cannot answer the Class A question — “That&#x27;s hard to answer. Aiming for the upper classes means forcing everyone… I&#x27;m sorry, I need to think on it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Adjusts his position so Ayanokōji can read the manual comfortably — “small acts of consideration” noted from the other side.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Carries her heart-bedazzled gifts in his pack and confirms it — “Spot on. How&#x27;d you guess?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Greets Kanzaki by name and accepts the apology for the early visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Coming from you, that honestly makes me really happy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Plans the sleeping-arrangement poll at the river, then after roll call assigns roles to the reliable students — Class D&#x27;s point-saving start.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 3  the corn report at base camp when ayanokoji cuts out of yamauchi s rant to reach him  gets the corn report first hand  soon afterward students are organized into a team that brings the harvest back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At base camp when Ayanokōji cuts out of Yamauchi’s rant to reach him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets the corn report first-hand; soon afterward students are organized into a team that brings the harvest back.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  the search and the secret called out of the tent by shinohara  he rouses the boys and runs the luggage inspection that ends with the stolen underwear in his own hands   ah  hirata kun  i m sorry  but can you please wake all of the boys  it s serious   i understand  i think if i shout  they ll come   i know that you re not the culprit  hirata kun  but for the time being  let s check the boys  luggage   well  there s no evidence that the boys stole it  maybe karuizawa lost it   i don t want to think there s a criminal among us   for now  we ll try gathering the guys together and talking it out  can you please give us a little time  the one boy exempt from her contempt  his word buys the others time   i don t doubt you guys  but we won t solve the problem like this   it might be better to just accept the baggage inspection with dignity and prove your innocence   of course  i ll open up my luggage first  opens his own bag first so that no other boy can refuse the inspection   as miserable as this might be  i think you guys ll have to do it  are you okay with that   we searched everyone s bags  none of us did it   yeah  there s no doubt  none of the boys are the culprit  the translation leaves the two reporting lines untagged after ike calls shinohara over  recorded here as the inspector s report   hey  hirata kun  could they have hidden it in their pockets  ike kun and yamauchi kun  and even ayanokouji kun were whispering a little earlier  it s got me curious   okay  if it convinces the girls  fine  however  if i don t find anything  i want you to stop investigating the boys   i m sorry  it ll be over soon  pats ayanokoji down  feels the cloth in his back pocket  and reports finding nothing  does not doubt him for a moment  yet keeps the finding to himself   ayanokouji kun doesn t have them either   those three didn t take them   did you take karuizawa s underwear  ayanokouji kun   i believe you  you re not that kind of person  but why did you have them in your pocket   if it s all right with you  may i hold onto the underwear   in the worst case scenario  if i m made out to be the culprit  i would take the least amount of damage  i am her boyfriend  more or less  takes the underwear into a vinyl toilet bag   the joker in a deck of cards   i see  so it definitely wasn t you  but i don t think ike kun or yamauchi kun did it  either  if they were the culprits  they probably wouldn t put the underwear in their own bags  they would have hidden it in another place   but we did find out one piece of bad news here  if the underwear came out of ike kun s bag  then there s a high chance that the culprit is someone in our class   i believe you re not the culprit  ayanokouji kun  that s why i saved you   but that s not all i want to say  i want you to help me find the real culprit  ayanokouji kun   i think people  both guys and girls  will be uneasy until the thief s found  to be honest  it would probably be best if i found the culprit  but it looks like it ll be difficult to get everyone together   thank you  thank you  ayanokouji kun   if you do happen to find the culprit  i want you to tell me first  i definitely do not want you to tell anyone else   if that information becomes public knowledge  our class will suffer a huge blow  i want to avoid that  that s why i want to find a peaceful method of settling things with the culprit  if it s coming from me  i think that we ll be able to resolve the issue through talking   hide it  that s a poor choice of words  but there s nothing i can do about it if people take it that way  even if one of the guys turns out to the be the culprit  i think it s better that the truth be concealed  the printed line reads  turns out to the be the culprit    kept as printed  widens his eyes while making the appeal for secrecy  the narration calls his calm almost too calm  a little eerie   thank you  well then  i ll be getting back to work  the narration marks one contradiction  right after saying he believes ayanokoji  he insists the truth be concealed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.159–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Called out of the tent by Shinohara, he rouses the boys and runs the luggage inspection that ends with the stolen underwear in his own hands.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Ah, Hirata-kun. I’m sorry, but can you please wake all of the boys? It’s serious,”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand. I think if I shout, they’ll come.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “I know that you’re not the culprit, Hirata-kun. But for the time being, let’s check the boys’ luggage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s no evidence that the boys stole it. Maybe Karuizawa lost it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want to think there’s a criminal among us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For now, we’ll try gathering the guys together and talking it out. Can you please give us a little time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The one boy exempt from her contempt; his word buys the others time.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t doubt you guys, but we won’t solve the problem like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It might be better to just accept the baggage inspection with dignity and prove your innocence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. I’ll open up my luggage first,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens his own bag first so that no other boy can refuse the inspection.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As miserable as this might be, I think you guys’ll have to do it. Are you okay with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We searched everyone’s bags. None of us did it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. There’s no doubt. None of the boys are the culprit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the two reporting lines untagged after Ike calls Shinohara over; recorded here as the inspector’s report.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata-kun. Could they have hidden it in their pockets? Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun, and even Ayanokouji-kun were whispering a little earlier. It’s got me curious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. If it convinces the girls, fine. However, if I don’t find anything, I want you to stop investigating the boys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. It’ll be over soon,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pats Ayanokōji down, feels the cloth in his back pocket, and reports finding nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Does not doubt him for a moment, yet keeps the finding to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun doesn’t have them either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those three didn’t take them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you…take Karuizawa’s underwear, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you. You’re not that kind of person. But why did you have them in your pocket?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s all right with you, may I hold onto the underwear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the worst-case scenario, if I’m made out to be the culprit, I would take the least amount of damage. I am her boyfriend, more or less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the underwear into a vinyl toilet bag — the Joker in a deck of cards.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So it definitely wasn’t you. But I don’t think Ike-kun or Yamauchi-kun did it, either. If they were the culprits, they probably wouldn’t put the underwear in their own bags. They would have hidden it in another place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But we did find out one piece of bad news here. If the underwear came out of Ike-kun’s bag, then there’s a high chance that the culprit is someone in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re not the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun. That’s why I saved you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s not all I want to say. I want you to help me find the real culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think people, both guys and girls, will be uneasy until the thief’s found. To be honest, it would probably be best if I found the culprit, but it looks like it’ll be difficult to get everyone together…”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you! Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun!”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do happen to find the culprit, I want you to tell me first. I definitely do not want you to tell anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that information becomes public knowledge, our class will suffer a huge blow. I want to avoid that. That’s why I want to find a peaceful method of settling things with the culprit. If it’s coming from me, I think that we’ll be able to resolve the issue through talking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hide it? That’s a poor choice of words, but there’s nothing I can do about it if people take it that way. Even if one of the guys turns out to the be the culprit, I think it’s better that the truth be concealed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line reads “turns out to the be the culprit” — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Widens his eyes while making the appeal for secrecy; the narration calls his calm almost too calm, a little eerie.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Well then, I’ll be getting back to work.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration marks one contradiction: right after saying he believes Ayanokōji, he insists the truth be concealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6 1  the meeting that splits the camp runs the meeting where karuizawa s fear turns into a ban on the boys  and takes the mediator s role once more   could everyone please gather around  the opening call of the meeting is left untagged in the translation  the narration has his meeting already begun as ayanokoji steps out   we can t trust the guys  it s absolutely impossible for us to stay in the same place as them   but there would be problems if the guys and girls lived apart  don t you think  the test is almost over  because we re all friends  we need to believe in and cooperate with one another  the translation leaves this answer to karuizawa untagged  she shakes her head at it in the next line   you might be right  but we can t stand being in the same place as underwear thieves  he cannot force her back when the victim says the boys cannot be trusted   okay  i ll help  it might take some time  though  is that okay  the only boy she trusts  she blushes when he agrees to help her side   yeah  hirata kun is the only one we can trust   huh  hirata kun is not the culprit  what a stupid thing to say  why don t you go jump off a cliff   karuizawa san  it would be great if we could have another guy here help me out  is that okay  adopts the role of mediator once again when karuizawa is on the verge of losing her temper   b but how can i trust anyone other than you  hirata kun   i understand what everyone wants to say here  but i disagree with suspecting a classmate without evidence  there shouldn t be anyone in our class who d do such an awful thing   i don t know  but i don t want to doubt my classmates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Runs the meeting where Karuizawa’s fear turns into a ban on the boys, and takes the mediator’s role once more.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could everyone please gather around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “We can’t trust the guys. It’s absolutely impossible for us to stay in the same place as them!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But there would be problems if the guys and girls lived apart, don’t you think? The test is almost over. Because we’re all friends, we need to believe in and cooperate with one another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening call of the meeting is left untagged in the translation; the narration has his meeting already begun as Ayanokōji steps out.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves this answer to Karuizawa untagged; she shakes her head at it in the next line.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might be right. But we can’t stand being in the same place as underwear thieves!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He cannot force her back when the victim says the boys cannot be trusted.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I’ll help. It might take some time, though. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only boy she trusts; she blushes when he agrees to help her side.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, Hirata-kun is the only one we can trust.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Hirata-kun is not the culprit. What a stupid thing to say. Why don’t you go jump off a cliff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san, it would be great if we could have another guy here help me out. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Adopts the role of mediator once again when Karuizawa is on the verge of losing her temper.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “B-but…how can I trust anyone other than you, Hirata-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what everyone wants to say here, but I disagree with suspecting a classmate without evidence. There shouldn’t be anyone in our class who’d do such an awful thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know, but I don’t want to doubt my classmates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6 2 6 3  the stakes  the points  the fever pitches the girls  second tent at ayanokoji s side after the split  then is pulled away by karuizawa and the other girls  the narration opens on him  a really cool guy  principled  taking the initiative on troublesome work and answering opponents respectfully   i m sorry  i ve put you in a tough spot again   oh  it s not all bad  i do it freely   work so hard  i don t intend to work all that hard  i just do what needs to be done   i think this special test isn t actually some kind of battle  but more an important opportunity for us all to become closer  that s why i want to cherish this moment  i m glad to work hard for that  works the stakes beside him and gets the straight answer about why he works so hard   ah  i still have work left to do  though   no  but it s hard for one person to  the printed line ends in a broken  glyph   kept as printed   s sorry  thank you  i ll be right back  is pulled off the stakes by the girls and left to ayanokoji  who finishes the work alone   exactly  trustworthy hirata kun has kept his mouth shut about it   karuizawa san reported this to hirata kun  so he definitely knew about it  but you didn t know  nor did he inform anyone else  i think he absolutely should have shared this information  kept quiet about the girls  twelve point spending  known to him through karuizawa s report","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.180–189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pitches the girls’ second tent at Ayanokōji’s side after the split, then is pulled away by Karuizawa and the other girls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. I’ve put you in a tough spot again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, it’s not all bad. I do it freely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Work so hard? I don’t intend to work all that hard. I just do what needs to be done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration opens on him: a really cool guy, principled, taking the initiative on troublesome work and answering opponents respectfully.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think this special test isn’t actually some kind of battle, but more an important opportunity for us all to become closer. That’s why I want to cherish this moment. I’m glad to work hard for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Works the stakes beside him and gets the straight answer about why he works so hard.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I still have work left to do, though,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, but it’s hard for one person to¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line ends in a broken¾ glyph — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. Thank you. I’ll be right back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is pulled off the stakes by the girls and left to Ayanokōji, who finishes the work alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. Trustworthy Hirata-kun has kept his mouth shut about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san reported this to Hirata-kun, so he definitely knew about it. But you didn’t know, nor did he inform anyone else. I think he absolutely should have shared this information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kept quiet about the girls’ twelve-point spending, known to him through Karuizawa’s report.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6 4  the last forage reports a quiet night  then sorts the class into teams for one last search for food   i m glad  we haven t had any incidents   would it be better if we went  too   no  ike kun  sudou kun  i want you two to continue fishing  we don t have enough time to instruct the other students how to do it  keeps ike and sudou on the river and sets the search groups by volunteers  with ayanokoji as backup","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.192–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reports a quiet night, then sorts the class into teams for one last search for food.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m glad. We haven’t had any incidents,”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Would it be better if we went, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. Ike-kun, Sudou-kun, I want you two to continue fishing. We don’t have enough time to instruct the other students how to do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps Ike and Sudou on the river and sets the search groups by volunteers, with Ayanokōji as backup.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6 7  the fire and the crack at the fire behind the temporary toilet   the survival manual was in his bag  and he takes the blame before the culprit   i m responsible for this  the manual was in my bag  we piled the bags up in front of the tent and i didn t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime  but first  we need to extinguish this fire properly  goes to the river to douse the fire instead of hunting the culprit  and crushes a plastic bottle in his fist   why  who could do something like this  why can t we all just get along  the eternal peacemaker cracks   the narration calls the shift in his personality rather terrifying   thank you   we need to discuss this incident properly   right  most of class d witnessed the fire  i m sure they ll want to know the truth  the reply carries no speaker tag  it sits under his own call to discuss  so it is recorded as his  hands his water to ayanokoji and goes into the circle to mediate   wait a minute  everyone  please  calm down  let s talk about this  stands dazed in the middle of the confrontation instead of stopping it   hirata  tell us what to do   why why is this happening  it s just like back then  the page never says what  back then  refers to  stares off into nothingness through the rising rain and does not notice ayanokoji approach   why was i doing this  why was i doing all this until now   ike s calling for you   rain   it d be good for you to help ike and the others  we have to keep our stuff dry   y yeah  we need to take care of everything quickly  sudou watches the shock from the side and names the danger of a breakdown before anyone else  since the test began he has carried one burden after another  the underwear theft and the fire have turned him unhinged and stormy as the weather","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the fire behind the temporary toilet — the survival manual was in his bag, and he takes the blame before the culprit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m responsible for this. The manual was in my bag. We piled the bags up in front of the tent and I didn’t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime. But first, we need to extinguish this fire properly…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why? Who could do something like this? Why can’t we all just get along?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes to the river to douse the fire instead of hunting the culprit, and crushes a plastic bottle in his fist.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The eternal peacemaker cracks — the narration calls the shift in his personality rather terrifying.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need…to discuss this incident properly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Most of Class D witnessed the fire. I’m sure they’ll want to know the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply carries no speaker tag; it sits under his own call to discuss, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands his water to Ayanokōji and goes into the circle to mediate.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute, everyone. Please, calm down. Let’s talk about this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands dazed in the middle of the confrontation instead of stopping it.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata, tell us what to do!”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why…why is this happening? It’s just like back then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page never says what “back then” refers to.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stares off into nothingness through the rising rain and does not notice Ayanokōji approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why was I doing this? Why was I doing all this until now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ike’s calling for you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rain…”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be good for you to help Ike and the others. We have to keep our stuff dry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-yeah. We need to take care of everything quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou watches the shock from the side and names the danger of a breakdown before anyone else.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Since the test began he has carried one burden after another; the underwear theft and the fire have turned him unhinged and stormy as the weather.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the rest area and the deck<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 7  the rest area and the deck brings paper cups to the rest area  thanks ayanokoji and sudou for the week  and carries the beach exchange with ryuuen until mashima s megaphone cuts it short   good work  both of you  thank you for everything you did this week  you really saved us  hands him and sudou the two paper cups he was carrying   i should be thanking you  you covered for me  the class loner  also  you covered for me being late for roll call  and the fact that horikita retired   i couldn t blame you when i heard the reason  besides  horikita san gave us some really important information   do you believe what she said   she isn t the type to speak irresponsibly  that s why you get along with her  right  the narration calls him the one who would protect an ally even if it risked his pure reputation   i d be lying if i said there wasn t any risk  but i had to help horikitasan   that s a friend   wait  what did you say  what are you talking about  finds class c emptied with the pair   ibuki nowhere on the sandy beach   ryuuen alone  cup in hand   oh  hey there  sycophants  what happened to suzune   i know you ve been chasing suzune s ass  we were together before  you know   throw that away for me   what a stupid thing to say  huh  pick up your own trash  jerk   but picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage   calm down  sudou kun  here  i ll throw it away  hurriedly picks up the cup sudou trampled   who are you  more importantly  where s suzune  i ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom   the next time you say something stupid  i ll kill you  sudou growled  jumps in and pulls sudou away from ryuuen before fists can fly   horikita san retired yesterday  she s not here   retired  suzune  she doesn t seem like that kind of girl  his reply is untagged and is recorded as his   i thought you retired  ryuuen kun  and the interrupted reply  that s  are left out as chapter attribution gaps  the broken three quarter mark is kept as printed   that s what we should be saying to you class c people  you used up all of your points  right  don t make us laugh   we have 125 points remaining  i think we ll be quite fine   so you re going to expose a class leader   hold on a minute  what are you talking about  huh  i if you re telling the truth  then   bwah ha ha ha  hey  check it out  you guys have zero points after all   i ll explain everything  well  ryuuen kun  if you ll excuse us  walks toward the boat with ike and sudou while sudou raises a middle finger at ryuuen   you jerk  kouenji  we lost thirty points because of you  you know what i m talking about  don t you   well  karuizawa san  i think you should talk to horikita san first  don t you agree   horikita san  do you have a minute  the line is attributed only to  he  he has just proposed the talk  so it is recorded as him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the rest area and the deck<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.240–246<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Brings paper cups to the rest area, thanks Ayanokōji and Sudou for the week, and carries the beach exchange with Ryuuen until Mashima’s megaphone cuts it short.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Good work, both of you. Thank you for everything you did this week. You really saved us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I should be thanking you. You covered for me, the class loner. Also, you covered for me being late for roll call, and the fact that Horikita retired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I couldn’t blame you when I heard the reason. Besides, Horikita-san gave us some really important information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him and Sudou the two paper cups he was carrying.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you believe what she said?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She isn’t the type to speak irresponsibly. That’s why you get along with her, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration calls him the one who would protect an ally even if it risked his pure reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d be lying if I said there wasn’t any risk, but I had to help Horikitasan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what did you say? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds Class C emptied with the pair — Ibuki nowhere on the sandy beach — Ryuuen alone, cup in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, hey there, sycophants. What happened to Suzune?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’ve been chasing Suzune’s ass. We were together before, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Throw that away for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a stupid thing to say. Huh? Pick up your own trash, jerk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Sudou-kun. Here, I’ll throw it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hurriedly picks up the cup Sudou trampled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you? More importantly, where’s Suzune? I’ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time you say something stupid, I’ll kill you,” Sudou growled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jumps in and pulls Sudou away from Ryuuen before fists can fly.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san retired yesterday. She’s not here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Retired? Suzune? She doesn’t seem like that kind of girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His reply is untagged and is recorded as his; “I thought you retired, Ryuuen-kun.” and the interrupted reply “That’s¾” are left out as chapter attribution gaps; the broken three-quarter mark is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what we should be saying to you Class C people. You used up all of your points, right? Don’t make us laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have 125 points remaining. I think we’ll be quite fine,”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re going to expose a class leader?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hold on a minute. What are you talking about, huh?! I-If you’re telling the truth, then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bwah ha ha ha! Hey, check it out! You guys have zero points after all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll explain everything. Well, Ryuuen-kun, if you’ll excuse us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks toward the boat with Ike and Sudou while Sudou raises a middle finger at Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You jerk, Kouenji! We lost thirty points because of you. You know what I’m talking about, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, Karuizawa-san, I think you should talk to Horikita-san first, don’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is attributed only to “he”; he has just proposed the talk, so it is recorded as him.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 0  he pulls ayanokoji to lunch ship cabin  he draws ayanokoji out of his sea gazing and steers him toward lunch  cancelling karuizawa s plan to do it   hmm  you haven t been in the room all this time  have you   you might make more friends if you were a little more proactive  ayanokouji kun  though i suppose it s none of my business   that s not true  though  i mean  you have sudou kun and the guys  and horikita san   i m planning to meet up with karuizawa san and the others at 12 30 to have lunch  do you want to come with  i think it ll be really fun  wears  that eternal  optimistic smile  and won t leave a lone person alone  pushes past the refusals   i can understand that you re feeling hesitant  that s exactly why i want you to rely on me   i can eat with karuizawa san and the others any time  but i haven t really had many opportunities to eat together with you  ayanokouji kun  calls karuizawa to cancel on the spot  despite ayanokoji s half hearted protests   thank you for helping on the deserted island  i m sorry i didn t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit  ayanokouji kun   even so  i m grateful to you for helping  cancels their lunch without flinching  ayanokoji expects her to blame him later  and he doesn t seem to care","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ship cabin: he draws Ayanokōji out of his sea-gazing and steers him toward lunch, cancelling Karuizawa’s plan to do it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? You haven’t been in the room all this time, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You might make more friends if you were a little more proactive, Ayanokouji-kun. Though I suppose it’s none of my business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s not true, though. I mean, you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to meet up with Karuizawa-san and the others at 12:30 to have lunch. Do you want to come with? I think it’ll be really fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wears “that eternal, optimistic smile” and won’t leave a lone person alone; pushes past the refusals.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can understand that you’re feeling hesitant. That’s exactly why I want you to rely on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can eat with Karuizawa-san and the others any time, but I haven’t really had many opportunities to eat together with you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Karuizawa to cancel on the spot, despite Ayanokōji’s half-hearted protests.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for helping on the deserted island. I’m sorry I didn’t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I’m grateful to you for helping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Cancels their lunch without flinching; Ayanokōji expects her to blame him later, and he doesn’t seem to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 0  the ask  be the bridge to horikita top deck restaurant  over lunch he finally names his ask   ayanokoji as the bridge to horikita   honestly  there s something i d like your advice on   i wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach horikita san  after all  class d will have to come together and work hard in the future  and i think horikita san will be indispensable   yes  i do understand  of course  horikita san only opens herself up to you  ayanokouji kun  wants his own hand hidden    then  pretend i never spoke to you   but i can t come up with anything else right now  i don t think i have the confidence to speak with horikita san  let alone persuade her  this is my last resort   i should probably reconsider how to do this  horikita san seems very fastidious and hypercritical  how do you manage to get along with her  ayanokouji kun  has  over forty friends  yet is frustrated at missing a connection with one particular student   my plan was really short sighted   when ayanokoji calls the timing too soon   sorry  i invited you out to eat and made it all about me  well  let s eat  shall we  notices karuizawa approaching and shoots ayanokoji a nonplussed look before the girls close ranks  wants her friendship first  then a working relationship  and lacks the confidence to ask her directly  she arrives with her girls and takes the table back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.17–20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Top-deck restaurant: over lunch he finally names his ask — Ayanokōji as the bridge to Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Honestly, there’s something I’d like your advice on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach Horikita-san. After all, Class D will have to come together and work hard in the future, and I think Horikita-san will be indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. I do understand, of course. Horikita-san only opens herself up to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Wants his own hand hidden — “Then, pretend I never spoke to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> “But I can’t come up with anything else right now. I don’t think I have the confidence to speak with Horikita-san, let alone persuade her. This is my last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should probably reconsider how to do this. Horikita-san seems very fastidious and hypercritical. How do you manage to get along with her, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has “over forty friends” yet is frustrated at missing a connection with one particular student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My plan was really short-sighted.” (when Ayanokōji calls the timing too soon)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I invited you out to eat and made it all about me. Well, let’s eat, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Karuizawa approaching and shoots Ayanokōji a nonplussed look before the girls close ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Wants her friendship first, then a working relationship, and lacks the confidence to ask her directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She arrives with her girls and takes the table back.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the monopolised floor and the wished-for partner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  the monopolised floor and the wished for partner named through the floor s movements   karuizawa has him  and ayanokoji keeps circling back to the roommate  after karuizawa monopolized hirata  ayanokoji decides to return to his room  on the kouenji corridor scene  hirata would probably try to speak with him  but he d most likely be brushed off  he heads back to where hirata and yukimura  his other roommates  would be  a hallway question confirms the roommates  ayanokoji with hirata  kouenji  and yukimura  karuizawa s briefing complaint  what about hiratakun  or the other girls  she hates the team of boys   though being with hirata kun would be fine  she wails that hirata kun would have been so much better  the professor offers to surpass the good hirata dono with three heads  she calls out to hirata kun about something she wanted to talk about  then strides off   probably going to complain to him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the monopolised floor and the wished-for partner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–22, p.24, p.26, p.35–37, p.50<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named through the floor’s movements — Karuizawa has him, and Ayanokōji keeps circling back to the roommate.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After Karuizawa monopolized Hirata, Ayanokōji decides to return to his room.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the Kouenji corridor scene, Hirata would probably try to speak with him, but he’d most likely be brushed off.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He heads back to where Hirata and Yukimura, his other roommates, would be.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A hallway question confirms the roommates: Ayanokōji with Hirata, Kouenji, and Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa’s briefing complaint: what about Hiratakun? Or the other girls?<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She hates the team of boys — though being with Hirata-kun would be fine.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She wails that Hirata-kun would have been so much better; the Professor offers to surpass the good Hirata-dono with three heads.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She calls out to Hirata-kun about something she wanted to talk about, then strides off — probably going to complain to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations in the third deck cabin he straightens his luggage  puts on his uniform  and wakes ayanokoji for the evening s meetings   i m sorry  did i wake you   would you like to come with me  i was thinking the school s message should be coming pretty soon  already knows the test s specifics   yukimura told him over their meal   and several students have come to talk it through with him   did you notice anything  ayanokouji kun  if it s okay  i d like you to share it with me   well  i was wondering why the explanations are so scattered  i thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group  but after thinking about it  i don t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once  plans to ask a teacher directly about the staged briefings  wakes him  walks him down  gets only a deflection for his troubles  his inside source on the rabbit rules","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the third-deck cabin he straightens his luggage, puts on his uniform, and wakes Ayanokōji for the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. Did I wake you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Would you like to come with me? I was thinking the school’s message should be coming pretty soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did you notice anything, Ayanokouji-kun? If it’s okay, I’d like you to share it with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Already knows the test’s specifics — Yukimura told him over their meal — and several students have come to talk it through with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I was wondering why the explanations are so…scattered. I thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group, but after thinking about it, I don’t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Plans to ask a teacher directly about the staged briefings.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wakes him, walks him down, gets only a deflection for his troubles.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His inside source on the Rabbit rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the monopolised floor and the wished-for partner<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering second deck meeting place  he names the waiting students for ayanokoji  then stands inside the katsuragi horikita ryuen current   it doesn t seem like all of these people are in my group   that s morimiya kun  from class a  and that one near the elevator is tokitou kun  from class c   the well connected answer   yes  though if i m with you  kanzaki kun  and katsuragi kun  struggle has to be inevitable   answering kanzaki s sympathy   don t worry  no matter who is in my group  i ll do my best   to katsuragi  positive as always  positive through the threat display  kushida reads his steadiness as the sign that the battle will be grueling  addressed as the group s class a anchor  the class b boy who spots him landed in trouble  she finds him amid the gathering and takes his composure for reassurance  both summoned to the same 20 40 meeting   the team katsuragi named","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck meeting place: he names the waiting students for Ayanokōji, then stands inside the Katsuragi–Horikita–Ryūen current.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It doesn’t seem like all of these people are in my group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s Morimiya-kun, from Class A. And that one near the elevator is Tokitou-kun, from Class C.” (the well-connected answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. Though if I’m with you, Kanzaki-kun, and Katsuragi-kun, struggle has to be inevitable.” (answering Kanzaki’s sympathy)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. No matter who is in my group, I’ll do my best.” (to Katsuragi, positive as always)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Positive through the threat display; Kushida reads his steadiness as the sign that the battle will be grueling.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Addressed as the group’s Class A anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The Class B boy who spots him landed in trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She finds him amid the gathering and takes his composure for reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Both summoned to the same 20:40 meeting — the team Katsuragi named.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  named on the dragon roster and in the ichinose comparison roster line only in the cafe half  p 84 he appears as a comparison point inside the rabbit room  dragon groupmate with kushida    both excellent students  and representatives of our class  with horikita they are the strongest hand class d could deal  ichinose s persuasion is contrasted with his and kushida s  even they  might find themselves outmatched  despite their overabundance of friends  dragon groupmate on the biased list  the other class d name on the dragon roster  named in her praise as a floor under her people work","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64, p.84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Roster line only in the café half; p.84 he appears as a comparison point inside the Rabbit room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Dragon groupmate with Kushida — “both excellent students, and representatives of our class”; with Horikita they are the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose’s persuasion is contrasted with his and Kushida’s: even they “might find themselves outmatched, despite their overabundance of friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The other Class D name on the Dragon roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named in her praise as a floor under her people-work.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p65-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the measure, the check, and the conduit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p65-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  the measure  the check  and the conduit named in the grade theory comparison and the list of people who might steady horikita  the score theory line puts the gap between the speaker and the professor beside the one with hirata  despite powerful foes  horikita was indomitable   hirata and kushida would hopefully keep her in check  on the karuizawa class c friction  karuizawa already had hirata  though  he says they re heading back too   he wants to talk to hirata about some things  he wanted opinions from people other than hirata and horikita on the strange test  a strong character group might work if people like hirata and ichinose took the lead  the class b ready alliance pattern was like how hirata operated  the joke read of ibuki  maybe she was communicating with hirata in real time so he could listen to their conversation  whatever her reputation  she and hirata often brought the class together   and hirata was always hirata  no matter the situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the measure, the check, and the conduit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.65, p.77, p.95–97, p.106, p.108–109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the grade-theory comparison and the list of people who might steady Horikita.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The score-theory line puts the gap between the speaker and the Professor beside the one with Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Despite powerful foes, Horikita was indomitable — Hirata and Kushida would hopefully keep her in check.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the Karuizawa–Class C friction: Karuizawa already had Hirata, though.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He says they’re heading back too — he wants to talk to Hirata about some things.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He wanted opinions from people other than Hirata and Horikita on the strange test.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A strong-character group might work if people like Hirata and Ichinose took the lead; the Class B ready-alliance pattern was like how Hirata operated.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The joke read of Ibuki: maybe she was communicating with Hirata in real time so he could listen to their conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whatever her reputation, she and Hirata often brought the class together — and Hirata was always Hirata, no matter the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  3 5  the trusted conduit waiting when ayanokoji returns near midnight  shares the yukimura info chat  whispers the two known vips  and shows them by phone   good work today  ayanokouji kun  you re rather late  said hirata   i m sure you re tired  but if you re up for it  do you mind talking with me  he asked   the simultaneous ask with ayanokoji   huh  what did you want to ask me  said hirata   i just chatted a bit with yukimura kun  we decided to share information about the test  said hirata   i would ve been glad if kouenji kun participated  but he unfortunately declined  said hirata   kouenji is participating in a group  after all  students are required to participate  and points are taken away if a student fails to participate  said hirata   trust hirata to read the rules thoroughly   to tell you the truth  i got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the vips in their groups  he whispered   that s  i can t say  they only told me because they trust me   yeah  you re right  wait just a moment   agreeing to phone for the names  puts two names on the screen for yukimura and ayanokoji    dragon group  kushida san  horse group  minami kun    and erases them immediately after   don t worry  everything is all right  said hirata   yeah  i think your logic follows  they certainly haven t talked to me about it  but they might ve consulted someone else  after all  there s a high risk of being discovered if you talk  hirata said   we still don t know anything yet  he probably had his own ideas  replied hirata   on kouenji s sudden traitor move  his phone starts beeping continuously as classmates demand to know what happened  he stays the generous reader of the situation  the info chat partner before ayanokoji arrived  declined the huddle  then ended his own group under him  named dragon vip on his screen  trusts him with the erased screen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting when Ayanokōji returns near midnight; shares the Yukimura info chat, whispers the two known VIPs, and shows them by phone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Good work today, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re rather late,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sure you’re tired, but if you’re up for it, do you mind talking with me?” he asked. (the simultaneous ask with Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh? What did you want to ask me?” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just chatted a bit with Yukimura-kun. We decided to share information about the test,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I would’ve been glad if Kouenji-kun participated, but he unfortunately declined,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kouenji is participating in a group. After all, students are required to participate, and points are taken away if a student fails to participate,” said Hirata. (trust Hirata to read the rules thoroughly)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the VIPs in their groups,” he whispered.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… I can’t say. They only told me because they trust me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, you’re right. Wait just a moment.” (agreeing to phone for the names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Puts two names on the screen for Yukimura and Ayanokōji — “Dragon Group, Kushida-san. Horse Group, Minami-kun.” — and erases them immediately after.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. Everything is all right,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I think your logic follows. They certainly haven’t talked to me about it, but they might’ve consulted someone else. After all, there’s a high risk of being discovered if you talk,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We still don’t know anything yet. He probably had his own ideas,” replied Hirata. (on Kouenji’s sudden traitor move)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His phone starts beeping continuously as classmates demand to know what happened; he stays the generous reader of the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The info-chat partner before Ayanokōji arrived.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Declined the huddle, then ended his own group under him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Trusts him with the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p65-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the measure, the check, and the conduit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: one of the two ringleaders<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p116-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  one of the two ringleaders named as the first of the pair ayanokoji considers using  the ringleaders were hirata and kushida   using them is muttered as impossible with three days left","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: one of the two ringleaders<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the first of the pair Ayanokōji considers using.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The ringleaders were Hirata and Kushida — using them is muttered as impossible with three days left.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the route around him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p126-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  the route around him named as the contact to avoid when asking about karuizawa  ayanokoji s note  hirata probably remembered he d passed on the lunch with karuizawa  so he wanted to avoid asking him about this   the suggestion on the page is to talk to hirata kun instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the route around him<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.126<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the contact to avoid when asking about Karuizawa.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s note: Hirata probably remembered he’d passed on the lunch with Karuizawa, so he wanted to avoid asking him about this — the suggestion on the page is to talk to Hirata-kun instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: one of the two ringleaders<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 0 4 1  the absent roommate and the corridor pass named as the better source on dragon group detail while ayanokoji walks back to an empty room  then passes ayanokoji in the dragon doorway on day two  the planned mining target    hirata would likely approach this test from a different perspective than horikita  set up as the alternate dragon group lens beside her  brief exchanged looks as they pass in the doorway   no line  leaves the room with her before the three way opens to ichinose and ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.131–144<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the better source on Dragon-group detail while Ayanokōji walks back to an empty room, then passes Ayanokōji in the Dragon doorway on day two.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The planned mining target — “Hirata would likely approach this test from a different perspective than Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Set up as the alternate Dragon-group lens beside her.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> brief exchanged looks as they pass in the doorway — no line.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Leaves the room with her before the three-way opens to Ichinose and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the route around him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p156-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the dating arithmetic and the stairwell taunt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p156-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  the dating arithmetic and the stairwell taunt named as the boyfriend in the room s seating math around karuizawa  she could say it with a straight face because she was already dating hirata  karuizawa was dating hirata whether machida knew it or not  would hirata have been able to get them a little more organized    her influence grew by becoming hirata s girlfriend  the stairwell taunt on who she d call  hirata kun  machida kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p156-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the dating arithmetic and the stairwell taunt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.156–157, p.164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the boyfriend in the room’s seating math around Karuizawa.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She could say it with a straight face because she was already dating Hirata; Karuizawa was dating Hirata whether Machida knew it or not.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Would Hirata have been able to get them a little more organized? — her influence grew by becoming Hirata’s girlfriend.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The stairwell taunt on who she’d call: Hirata-kun? Machida-kun?<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: the absent roommate and the corridor pass<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei morofuji-rika manabe-shiho horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 4  the farce ends at the vending machine slips out of the room at 2 a m  into ayanokoji s hallway trap  takes him to karuizawa s meeting  and ends the fake dating on the spot when revenge is refused  the night walk   did i wake you     karuizawa contacted you  didn t she    tasks him with saving her   then  i honestly find you a little weird  you kind of creep me out   did i wake you  or were you already awake  he asked   why would you think that  this was the first time i ve left the room at night   karuizawa contacted you  didn t she   ayanokoji  reported exchange   do you happen to know something about it  he asked   she asked me to report on everything that happens in the rabbit group  including karuizawa s situation   his paraphrase of horikita s order   reported   what kind of information does she want  he asked   i don t know what i can tell you  honestly  i have to consider karuizawa san s feelings   ayanokouji kun  i m sure you won t say anything unnecessary  but what i m about to tell you is extremely delicate  also  karuizawa san might refuse to talk and head back to her room  please understand that first  he said  brings ayanokoji against her  alone  wish  holds the no violence line  reveals the farce    i ve told you from the start that we aren t really boyfriend and girlfriend   i asked him to come  said hirata   you did  hirata kun  why  i told you i wanted to talk alone   her line  tagged to him in exchange   i know  but karuizawa san  i was worried about what you told me earlier  that s why i thought it might be a good idea to bring ayanokouji kun  since he seems to understand the situation  i m sorry for not telling you first   if you want  we can be alone  but when we spoke earlier  you never said anything about it having to be just the two of us   you were telling me about a fight with manabe san from class c  is it true  he asked   ayanokouji kun  did you know about the fight with manabe san and the others  he asked   from what karuizawa san has told me  it seems like the girls were   making false accusations  they took her to a deserted spot and started hounding her for answers  they were on the verge of using violence  hirata said   i see   if manabe san and her friends got violent with you  we definitely need to take action  i absolutely cannot allow violence  he continued   i see  so that s why you told me  he said   karuizawa san asked me to take revenge on manabe san and her friends   his report of her request   because this isn t like you  karuizawa san  you aren t a violent   person  hirata answered    refuses eye for an eye while still claiming allyship   yes  i do  but i don t believe in an eye for an eye  you know that  don t you   let s think this through  if possible  let s find a way to get along with manabe san and her friends  he said   no reason  didn t this start because you had an issue with morofuji san  karuizawa  names morofuji san as the origin    hirata said morofuji  but he probably meant rika  that must ve been her last name  morning plan  tell them to stop  and tell them karuizawa will apologize   she refuses  so he will not help on her terms   of course i ll protect you  but i can t just hurt manabe san and her friends for no real reason  let s try to find a way to resolve things peacefully  through discussion   if that s the case  then i can t help you  i m sorry   it doesn t matter what the reason is  i can t do what you want  you re one of my classmates  karuizawa san  if you re in trouble  i ll help you  protect you  but i can t hurt someone else to do that  even if they re from class c  he said   liar  you ve known this was my stance since the beginning  he stood up   i ve told you from the start that we aren t really boyfriend and girlfriend  i don t mind pretending to go out with you  but i definitely won t fight a war for you   because we need a new option now  i want to help you  he said   ayanokouji kun  do you have any ideas  asked hirata   ayanokouji kun  i have my limits  i can t do everything  please understand that  he said   yes  i m karuizawa san s ally  and i m your ally as well  ayanokouji kun  however  my priorities might change depending on the situation  you re far more capable than everyone thinks  hirata observed   you re exactly right  we weren t really dating  we were going out because we both felt that it was necessary  i suppose you consider that contradictory  he answered  the bridge story is the cover he accepts   saving karuizawa san will give our class a lead   ayanokouji kun  i have to be very honest  but  well  this is going to sound very rude  but i honestly find you a little weird  you kind of creep me out  i m sorry if that offends you   i ve been watching you since school started  the ayanokouji kun back then and the ayanokouji kun now are like two different people  your presence  the words you use  it s like you have two different personalities  frighteningly observant   the two personality read is the sharpest student diagnosis of ayanokoji so far in the volume   well  i suppose horikita san must ve determined that saving karuizawa san will give our class a lead  he reasoned  the four month farce as mutual necessity  she proposed  he honored   host  and  parasite  is ayanokoji s caste reading of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.170–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Slips out of the room at 2 a.m. into Ayanokōji’s hallway trap, takes him to Karuizawa’s meeting, and ends the fake dating on the spot when revenge is refused.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"morofuji-rika.html\">Morofuji Rika<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did I wake you? Or were you already awake?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why would you think that? This was the first time I’ve left the room at night.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Karuizawa contacted you, didn’t she?” (Ayanokōji; reported exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>40 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The night walk: “Did I wake you?” → “Karuizawa contacted you, didn’t she?” → tasks him with saving her — then “I honestly find you a little weird. You kind of creep me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170-178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you happen to know something about it?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She asked me to report on everything that happens in the Rabbit group, including Karuizawa’s situation.” (his paraphrase of Horikita’s order — reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What kind of information does she want?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what I can tell you, honestly. I have to consider Karuizawa-san’s feelings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, I’m sure you won’t say anything unnecessary, but what I’m about to tell you is extremely delicate. Also, Karuizawa-san might refuse to talk and head back to her room. Please understand that first,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Brings Ayanokōji against her “alone” wish; holds the no-violence line; reveals the farce — “I’ve told you from the start that we aren’t really boyfriend and girlfriend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171-176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I asked him to come,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You did, Hirata-kun? Why? I told you I wanted to talk alone.” (her line, tagged to him in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know. But Karuizawa-san, I was worried about what you told me earlier. That’s why I thought it might be a good idea to bring Ayanokouji-kun, since he seems to understand the situation. I’m sorry for not telling you first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want, we can be alone. But when we spoke earlier, you never said anything about it having to be just the two of us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were telling me about a fight with Manabe-san from Class C. Is it true?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, did you know about the fight with Manabe-san and the others?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what Karuizawa-san has told me, it seems like the girls were … making false accusations. They took her to a deserted spot and started hounding her for answers. They were on the verge of using violence,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.172-173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Manabe-san and her friends got violent with you, we definitely need to take action. I absolutely cannot allow violence,” he continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So that’s why you told me,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san asked me to take revenge on Manabe-san and her friends.” (his report of her request)<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Because this isn’t like you, Karuizawa-san. You aren’t a violent … person,” Hirata answered. — refuses eye for an eye while still claiming allyship.<span class=\"pg\">p.173-174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, I do. But I don’t believe in an eye for an eye. You know that, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s think this through. If possible, let’s find a way to get along with Manabe-san and her friends,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No reason? Didn’t this start because you had an issue with Morofuji-san, Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Names Morofuji-san as the origin — “Hirata said Morofuji, but he probably meant Rika. That must’ve been her last name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Morning plan: tell them to stop, and tell them Karuizawa will apologize — she refuses, so he will not help on her terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.174-176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll protect you. But I can’t just hurt Manabe-san and her friends for no real reason. Let’s try to find a way to resolve things peacefully, through discussion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the case, then I can’t help you. I’m sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter what the reason is. I can’t do what you want. You’re one of my classmates, Karuizawa-san. If you’re in trouble, I’ll help you, protect you. But I can’t hurt someone else to do that, even if they’re from Class C,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “‘Liar’? You’ve known this was my stance since the beginning.” He stood up.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve told you from the start that we aren’t really boyfriend and girlfriend. I don’t mind pretending to go out with you, but I definitely won’t fight a war for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because we need a new option now. I want to help you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, do you have any ideas?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I have my limits. I can’t do everything. Please understand that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’m Karuizawa-san’s ally, and I’m your ally as well, Ayanokouji-kun. However, my priorities might change depending on the situation. You’re far more capable than everyone thinks,” Hirata observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re exactly right. We weren’t really dating. We were going out because we both felt that it was necessary. I suppose you consider that contradictory,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The bridge story is the cover he accepts; “saving Karuizawa-san will give our class a lead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170-178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I have to be very honest, but… Well, this is going to sound very rude, but I honestly find you a little weird. You kind of creep me out. I’m sorry if that offends you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve been watching you since school started. The Ayanokouji-kun back then and the Ayanokouji-kun now are like two different people. Your presence, the words you use… It’s like you have two different personalities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Frighteningly observant — the two-personality read is the sharpest student diagnosis of Ayanokōji so far in the volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well. I suppose Horikita-san must’ve determined that saving Karuizawa-san will give our class a lead,” he reasoned.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The four-month farce as mutual necessity: she proposed, he honored; “host” and “parasite” is Ayanokōji’s caste reading of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p156-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the dating arithmetic and the stairwell taunt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4 4  sugimura and the last class d vip explains the boyfriend farce as anti bullying penance  tells the sugimura window story  pledges confidentiality  then reveals he knows the last class d vip   yeah  but i do think you re amazing  ayanokouji kun  you re different from ike kun and yamauchi kun   even if you re just following horikita san s orders  you re still the one talking to me right now  ayanokouji kun  it isn t as though horikita gave you a list of prepared responses  i think that you show clear  well reasoned logic  that s not something you can pretend to have  the sharpest compliment of ayanokoji s performed normalcy   logic cannot be scripted   you ve already said as much  but i agreed to act like karuizawa san s boyfriend so she could protect herself  that s what she wanted  she said she wanted me to save her  it might be a little difficult for you to imagine  but throughout her elementary and junior high years  she was viciously bullied   of course  i only met karuizawa san after she started school here  but i understood  people who are bullied give off a unique vibe  that s why i agreed to go out with her  that way  karuizawa san would free herself from her past by using her position as my girlfriend  i don t think that karuizawa san has been showing us her real personality  i think she s just desperately trying to act tough  the host bargain restated as protection  her real personality is the act   what was in it for me  karuizawa san wasn t being bullied  that s all i needed   i know you re not convinced  but that s the reason i did it  he continued   until my second year of junior high i was  for lack of a better word  a nobody  i didn t stand out at all   well  i wouldn t say that i was completely invisible  i did have friends  i had this one friend ever since i was little  a guy named sugimura kun  we were in the same class together for six years  throughout elementary school  we were neighbors  too  we walked to and from school together every day  hirata spoke like he was recalling some fleeting memory   when we started junior high  we were put into separate classes for the first time  at first  we kept going to school together just like we always had  gradually  we walked together less and less  i started to only hang out with other guys from my new class  that story probably sounds normal enough  i suppose   but you see  while i had my new friends  sugimura kun was getting bullied  hirata squeezed the can he was holding   yeah  i didn t do anything  i couldn t  i was afraid i d become their next target  i was afraid that my new  fun life would be destroyed  so i pretended not to see sugimura kun  my oldest friend   that day s burned into my memory  even now  after morning soccer practice  i returned to the classroom  when i got near the room  i saw that sugimura kun was already there  his face swollen  i decided to wait a bit before going in    perhaps sugimura kun saw how ugly my heart was  he didn t say a word  but it was almost like he was sending out a plea for help  that day  he jumped out of the classroom window  said hirata   he was declared brain dead  but even now  sugimura kun s parents believe he ll recover  they re waiting for him    when sugimura kun jumped  i realized something  by selfishly focusing so much on my own desires  i helped drive a treasured friend to his death  the origin of hirata yousuke   penance through saving others  named as the birth of the man   i don t think sugimura kun can be saved  but i wanted to atone  i figure the only way for me to do that is to save others  hirata said   of course i know that  i m not a hero or anything  but i want to save the people close to me  at the very least  i must help them  that s my penance for the sin i committed  he said   i understand that  it s probably why you re here with me right now  he answered   i never thought i d ever tell this story to anyone  nobody here knows the truth  that s why i chose this school  said hirata   will you and horikita san keep this confidential  he asked   then i ll believe in you two  our philosophies are similar  the confidentiality is a two person pact through her   oh  ayanokouji kun  there is one more thing i ve been hiding from you  i know the identity of the last vip from class d  the class d vip count closed from his side   withheld until the bargain is sealed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179–183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Explains the boyfriend farce as anti-bullying penance, tells the Sugimura window story, pledges confidentiality, then reveals he knows the last Class D VIP.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. But I do think you’re amazing, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even if you’re just following Horikita-san’s orders, you’re still the one talking to me right now, Ayanokouji-kun. It isn’t as though Horikita gave you a list of prepared responses. I think that you show clear, well-reasoned…”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’ve already said as much, but I agreed to act like Karuizawa-san’s boyfriend so she could protect herself. That’s what she wanted. She said she wanted me to save her. It might be a little difficult for you to imagine, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you’re just following Horikita-san’s orders, you’re still the one talking to me right now, Ayanokouji-kun. It isn’t as though Horikita gave you a list of prepared responses. I think that you show clear, well-reasoned logic. That’s not something you can pretend to have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The sharpest compliment of Ayanokōji’s performed normalcy — logic cannot be scripted.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve already said as much, but I agreed to act like Karuizawa-san’s boyfriend so she could protect herself. That’s what she wanted. She said she wanted me to save her. It might be a little difficult for you to imagine, but throughout her elementary and junior high years, she was viciously bullied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, I only met Karuizawa-san after she started school here. But I understood. People who are bullied give off a unique vibe. That’s why I agreed to go out with her. That way, Karuizawa-san would free herself from her past by using her position as my girlfriend. I don’t think that Karuizawa-san has been showing us her real personality. I think she’s just desperately trying to act tough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The host bargain restated as protection; her real personality is the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What was in it for me? Karuizawa-san wasn’t being bullied. That’s all I needed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’re not convinced, but that’s the reason I did it,” he continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Until my second year of junior high I was, for lack of a better word, a nobody. I didn’t stand out at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I wouldn’t say that I was completely invisible. I did have friends. I had this one friend ever since I was little, a guy named Sugimura-kun. We were in the same class together for six years, throughout elementary school. We were neighbors, too. We walked to and from school together every day.” Hirata spoke like he was recalling some fleeting memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we started junior high, we were put into separate classes for the first time. At first, we kept going to school together just like we always had. Gradually, we walked together less and less. I started to only hang out with other guys from my new class. That story probably sounds normal enough, I suppose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But you see, while I had my new friends, Sugimura-kun was getting bullied.” Hirata squeezed the can he was holding.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I didn’t do anything. I couldn’t. I was afraid I’d become their next target. I was afraid that my new, fun life would be destroyed. So I pretended not to see Sugimura-kun, my oldest friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That day’s burned into my memory, even now. After morning soccer practice, I returned to the classroom. When I got near the room, I saw that Sugimura-kun was already there, his face swollen. I decided to wait a bit before going in. … Perhaps Sugimura-kun saw how ugly my heart was. He didn’t say a word, but it was almost like he was sending out a plea for help. That day, he jumped out of the classroom window,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He was declared brain dead. But even now, Sugimura-kun’s parents believe he’ll recover. They’re waiting for him. … When Sugimura-kun jumped, I realized something. By selfishly focusing so much on my own desires, I helped drive a treasured friend to his death.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The origin of Hirata Yousuke — penance through saving others, named as the birth of the man.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think Sugimura-kun can be saved, but I wanted to atone. I figure the only way for me to do that is to save others,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I know that. I’m not a hero or anything. But I want to save the people close to me, at the very least. I must help them. That’s my penance for the sin I committed,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that. It’s probably why you’re here with me right now,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never thought I’d ever tell this story to anyone. Nobody here knows the truth. That’s why I chose this school,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you and Horikita-san keep this confidential?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I’ll believe in you two. Our philosophies are similar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The confidentiality is a two-person pact through her.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, Ayanokouji-kun. There is one more thing I’ve been hiding from you. I know the identity of the last VIP from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The Class D VIP count closed from his side — withheld until the bargain is sealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: the farce ends at the vending machine<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p184-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the instrument of the plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p184-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  the instrument of the plan named as the first call in the order that will spring the switchboard trap  the plan s order  contact hirata  then have him call karuizawa   postponing a little means he needs to make the call  after their conversation last night  hirata might be especially on his guard   but if he asked to speak with her alone  she d respond  the anonymous chat s read  she won t leave hirata kun s or machida kun s side for a while  over ten minutes before her arranged meeting with hirata  she sits early to calm herself   and hirata isn t going to hear her muttering  asked where s hirata kun  the answer is that he was supposed to meet her here   the plan was to use him to stop manabe and her friends  karuizawa stammers whether the news came from hirata kun   the reply that hirata is everyone s ally  for better or worse  and will help anyone  the promise to her  i will be much more reliable than hirata or machida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the instrument of the plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.184–186, p.189, p.195, p.198, p.201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the first call in the order that will spring the switchboard trap.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The plan’s order: contact Hirata, then have him call Karuizawa — postponing a little means he needs to make the call.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After their conversation last night, Hirata might be especially on his guard — but if he asked to speak with her alone, she’d respond.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The anonymous chat’s read: she won’t leave Hirata-kun’s or Machida-kun’s side for a while.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Over ten minutes before her arranged meeting with Hirata, she sits early to calm herself — and Hirata isn’t going to hear her muttering.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked where’s Hirata-kun, the answer is that he was supposed to meet her here — the plan was to use him to stop Manabe and her friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa stammers whether the news came from Hirata-kun — the reply that Hirata is everyone’s ally, for better or worse, and will help anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The promise to her: I will be much more reliable than Hirata or Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: Sugimura and the last Class D VIP<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the side he’s brought over<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 5  the side he s brought over named as the source of the dragon vip fact   and the man ayanokoji claims to have handled  he d already heard from hirata that kushida was the dragon group s vip  to horikita  i ve brought hirata over to our side   a lot of cooperation expected   and i ll handle him and maintain things  when hirata and the others left the room  he headed to the meeting alone  with half the period still to run","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the side he’s brought over<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207–208, p.210<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the source of the Dragon VIP fact — and the man Ayanokōji claims to have handled.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He’d already heard from Hirata that Kushida was the Dragon group’s VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> To Horikita: I’ve brought Hirata over to our side — a lot of cooperation expected — and I’ll handle him and maintain things.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> When Hirata and the others left the room, he headed to the meeting alone, with half the period still to run.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p184-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the instrument of the plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the paper, the survey, the model<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 5  5 2 5 3  the paper  the survey  the model the withheld vip knowledge named on the page  then the cafe approach about  that piece of paper  the group survey proving no class d betrayal  the timing deduction with horikita  and the puzzled dragon outcome  1 question  kept karuizawa s vip status from him and yukimura at first  the cafe line  that piece of paper you gave me  ties back to the earlier insurance   i m guessing you re talking about that piece of paper you gave me  right  ayanokouji kun  hirata s approach from behind made karuizawa jump in shock  makes her jump   the breakup scream is still fresh  she shifts but does not refuse the seat   excellent work on this test  both of you  may i sit  he asked   it s just about time  is horikita san still not here  shouldn t we contact her  asked hirata   ah  looks like she s here  said hirata   i was a little apprehensive about that  so i went around and asked people in the individual groups earlier  none of the guys said they turned traitor  hirata answered  the boys side survey across every group   the report class d trusts for the no betrayal read  natural rapport   he finishes her automation thought before she has to   so it s likely that all of the emails were sent together  in other words  the betrayal emails all came from one class  hirata finished her thought   they might have sent the emails at the exact same time as a way of showing off their supremacy  hirata added   how did you figure it out  asked hirata  his question contained a mixture of curiosity and fear  the fear curious question after the kushida reveal  later the pushback that he is not convinced of preternatural talent   i understand that ryuuen kun managed to discover the vips in class a  sure  but i m not convinced he has some kind of preternatural talent  still  how did dragon group end up with that result  asked hirata   what do you mean  the answer he protected all test sits at the centre of ayanokoji s 1  explanation  named as the defensive voter who could still move in the riskless half hour  no answer to his dragon question from anyone but ayanokoji   the table is stunned silent first","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p231-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the paper, the survey, the model<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.231–242<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The withheld VIP knowledge named on the page; then the café approach about “that piece of paper,” the group survey proving no Class D betrayal, the timing deduction with Horikita, and the puzzled Dragon Outcome #1 question.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m guessing you’re talking about that piece of paper you gave me. Right, Ayanokouji-kun?” Hirata’s approach from behind made Karuizawa jump in shock.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Excellent work on this test, both of you. May I sit?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s just about time. Is Horikita-san still not here? Shouldn’t we contact her?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Kept Karuizawa’s VIP status from him and Yukimura at first; the café line “that piece of paper you gave me” ties back to the earlier insurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.231, 234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Makes her jump — the breakup scream is still fresh; she shifts but does not refuse the seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, looks like she’s here,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was a little apprehensive about that, so I went around and asked people in the individual groups earlier. None of the guys said they turned traitor,” Hirata answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The boys-side survey across every group — the report Class D trusts for the no-betrayal read.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Natural rapport — he finishes her automation thought before she has to.<span class=\"pg\">p.236-237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s likely that all of the emails were sent together. In other words, the betrayal emails all came from one class.” Hirata finished her thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They might have sent the emails at the exact same time as a way of showing off their supremacy,” Hirata added.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did you figure it out?” asked Hirata. His question contained a mixture of curiosity and fear.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The fear-curious question after the Kushida reveal; later the pushback that he is not convinced of preternatural talent.<span class=\"pg\">p.239, 242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that Ryuuen-kun managed to discover the VIPs in Class A, sure, but I’m not convinced he has some kind of preternatural talent. Still, how did Dragon Group end up with that result?” asked Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The answer he protected all test sits at the centre of Ayanokōji’s 1% explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Named as the defensive voter who could still move in the riskless half hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No answer to his Dragon question from anyone but Ayanokōji — the table is stunned silent first.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the side he’s brought over<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
